-- title:
--   Flatness of the subscheme of I· J for invertible I
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ and $T$ be schemes and let $q\colon X\to T$ be a morphism. Let $I$ and $J$ be quasi-coherent ideal sheaves on $X$, given as `X.IdealSheafData`, i.e. by the assignment of an ideal $I(U)\subseteq \Gamma(X,U)$ to each affine open $U$ satisfying the usual compatibility. Assume $I$ is invertible in the sense of the predicate `IsInvertible`: for every point $x\in X$ there are an affine open $U$ of $X$ and a section $f\in\Gamma(X,U)$ with $x$ in the basic open $X.\mathrm{basicOpen}\,f$, together with a non-zero-divisor $g\in\Gamma(X, X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f)$ such that the ideal attached by $I$ to the affine open $X.\mathrm{affineBasicOpen}\,f$ is the principal ideal generated by $g$. Assume further that the closed immersion $I.\mathrm{subscheme}\iota$ of the closed subscheme cut out by $I$, followed by $q$, is flat, and likewise for $J$. The conclusion is that the closed immersion of the closed subscheme cut out by the product ideal sheaf $I\cdot J$, followed by $q$, is again flat. No hypothesis of invertibility is imposed on $J$.
--
--   This is the statement that adding a relative effective Cartier divisor to a closed subscheme that is flat over the base preserves flatness over the base, in the form needed for products of ideal sheaves. It is used, via iteration over products of powers of invertible ideal sheaves, in the construction underlying [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_comap_curveChange_pi_ofPoint_eq_mul_prod_pow_of_ker_le`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_comap_curveChange_pi_ofPoint_eq_mul_prod_pow_of_ker_le), where flatness of such subschemes of a curve over its base is required.
